* START-HISTORY:
* 28 Oct 26 dm  New (S.88 phase 2, S4).  TOOL.DICT's check.word, with its two halves, moved here so that TOOL.VOC and TOOL.FILES ask the same question of the name they build a
*               command from.
* 9 Nov 26 dm  S.186: why names the character that is wrong (15040 with $tk_badch); 12811 is left for a name that is empty or longer than 63.
* END-HISTORY
*
* START-DESCRIPTION:
*
*   call $tk_word(name, ok, why)
*
*     name   the word a page is about to put in a sentence as the NAME of a record, an item, a file or an index
*     ok     returned: 1 when the page may give it to a command, else 0
*     why    returned: null when ok; else the sentence that says why not (12811 or 12760)
*
*   Two questions, in this order.  (1) Is it only the characters $tk_run lets through (a-z, 0-9, dot, dash and underscore, 1 to 63 of them)?  $tk_run refuses the rest as well; the test
*   is here too so that a page can say so before it shows a box.  (2) Does the VOC of the account hold an entry of that name whose type is K (a keyword)?  A keyword is read by the
*   verb as the keyword and not as a name, whoever's record or file it was meant to be: DELETE VOC ALL asks "Delete all records in VOC?" and DELETE DICT file ALL and DELETE.INDEX
*   file ALL do the same for every item and every index, and the question goes to the output the page captures, so that nobody reads it.  A VOC entry is looked up the way a verb
*   looks it up (the VOC folds case), so a name in capitals is the same word.  Nothing is changed.
*
*   WHAT IT DOES NOT DO.  It does not say that the name exists or that the person may change it: the verb and the kernel's edit gates decide that.
*
* END-DESCRIPTION
*
* START-CODE

$internal
subroutine tk_word(name, ok, why)
$catalog $tk_word

   ok = (len(name) > 0 and len(name) <= 63)
   why = ''
   good = 'abcdefghijklmnopqrstuvwxyz0123456789._-'
   for q = 1 to len(name)
      if index(good, name[q, 1], 1) = 0 then ok = @false
   next q
   if not(ok) then
      * the name is what a person or a record gave: it is shown as printable ASCII only, a control or high byte as ?
      shown = ''
      nq = len(name)
      if nq > 40 then nq = 40
      for q = 1 to nq
         sq = seq(name[q, 1])
         if sq >= 32 and sq <= 126 then shown := name[q, 1] else shown := '?'
      next q
      call $tk_badch(name, bad.ch)                     ;* 9 Nov 26 (S.186): which character, in words
      if bad.ch = '' then
         why = sysmsg(12811, shown)                    ;* the length is what is wrong (none, or over 63)
      end else
         why = sysmsg(15040, shown, bad.ch)
      end
      return
   end

   open 'VOC' to kwf then
      read kwr from kwf, name then
         if upcase(kwr<1>[1, 1]) = 'K' then ok = @false
      end
      close kwf
   end
   if not(ok) then why = sysmsg(12760, name)

   return
end

* END-CODE
